WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:18.523
heard the horror in his father's voice and realized the book must be very important.

2
00:00:19.243 --> 00:00:22.966
He leaped toward it, hoping to grab it before Zing charred it.

3
00:00:23.546 --> 00:00:25.808
But Perda was closer—and faster too.

4
00:00:26.532 --> 00:00:31.896
She yanked the book away a split second before Zing's fiery breath set the wooden surface of the

5
00:00:31.936 --> 00:00:32.897
table aflame.

6
00:00:32.917 --> 00:00:41.063
"Bad boy, Zing," Asta scolded, snapping her fingers and magically dousing the fire.

7
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:42.764
"Thanks, Perda.

8
00:00:43.384 --> 00:00:45.686
That's the only known copy of that book.

9
00:00:46.527 --> 00:00:50.069
It would have been tricky to restore it, even using magic."

10
00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.352
Zann was relieved that the book was safe.

11
00:00:54.516 --> 00:00:59.400
The last time Zing had burned something important, Zann had been grounded for a whole week.

12
00:01:00.762 --> 00:01:05.206
And even though Magicians could do a lot of things with magic, they couldn't do everything.

13
00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:12.032
That book looked really old, which meant it was possible that nobody still living had read the entire

14
00:01:12.112 --> 00:01:17.917
thing. If that was the case, even the most powerful Restore spell couldn't bring it back if it

15
00:01:17.957 --> 00:01:18.697
was destroyed.

16
00:01:18.717 --> 00:01:25.010
"We should probably get out of here," Zann said, snapping his fingers to create a dragon harness.

17
00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:29.053
He grabbed Zing, who struggled and spit flames at him.

18
00:01:29.794 --> 00:01:32.796
But Zann ignored the burns and strapped on the harness.

19
00:01:33.596 --> 00:01:37.098
When it was secure, he quickly healed his burns with magic.

20
00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:41.461
"Okay, let's go," Darb said, and Gliss nodded.

21
00:01:42.222 --> 00:01:45.844
But Perda seemed to be totally focused on the book she was holding.

22
00:01:45.864 --> 00:01:47.806
"Hey, what is this?"

23
00:01:48.306 --> 00:01:50.868
she asked, peering down at the open page.

24
00:01:51.572 --> 00:01:53.573
"It looks like a poem or something."

25
00:01:53.593 --> 00:01:57.294
"We think it's a riddle," Zann's mother replied.

26
00:01:57.314 --> 00:02:01.896
"Those words used to be carved into the trunk of the Wormwood tree.

27
00:02:02.737 --> 00:02:05.298
Bark grew over the words long ago.

28
00:02:06.078 --> 00:02:11.880
But before that happened, a historian copied it into that book about the history of Wormwood."

29
00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.981
"That's cool," Zann said.

30
00:02:14.001 --> 00:02:15.522
"What does the riddle say?"

31
00:02:15.542 --> 00:02:18.123
"I'll read it out loud," Perda said.

32
00:02:18.863 --> 00:02:28.595
She cleared her throat and then began: "Bygone days lost to time's haze Yet visible to careful gaze

33
00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:35.278
Rooted in the depths of time Touch and see—no need to climb."

34
00:02:35.298 --> 00:02:38.559
"What in the worlds does that mean?"

35
00:02:39.019 --> 00:02:41.860
Gliss asked, furrowing her brow in confusion.

36
00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.642
"We're not sure yet," Nax said.

37
00:02:44.662 --> 00:02:50.084
"Zann's mother just found that book buried in an old trunk in the basement of the university library."

38
00:02:51.324 --> 00:02:52.065
Asta nodded.

39
00:02:52.085 --> 00:02:55.587
"I was beginning our research into the Wormwood tree."

40
00:02:56.368 --> 00:02:58.389
That was enough of an explanation for Zann.

41
00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:02.171
He wanted to have fun with the last few hours of his friends' visit.

42
00:03:02.752 --> 00:03:05.754
He didn't want to hear about another of his parents' work projects.

43
00:03:05.774 --> 00:03:07.655
"So where do you want to go?"

44
00:03:07.975 --> 00:03:08.896
he asked his friends.

45
00:03:08.916 --> 00:03:12.378
"Maybe we should check out the new other-worlds exhibit at the zoo."

46
00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:15.300
"Hold on."

47
00:03:15.981 --> 00:03:17.742
Perda was still peering at the book.

48
00:03:17.762 --> 00:03:20.444
"May I take a blink image of the riddle?

49
00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.521
It would be fun to try to puzzle it out."

50
00:03:23.541 --> 00:03:26.463
"Sure, go ahead," Nax said with a smile.

51
00:03:26.483 --> 00:03:28.584
"Let us know if you have any ideas!"

52
00:03:29.405 --> 00:03:31.025
Perda held the book up to her face.

53
00:03:31.045 --> 00:03:34.107
"Blink," she murmured as she blinked her eyes.

54
00:03:34.828 --> 00:03:37.169
A second later a sheet of paper appeared.

55
00:03:37.889 --> 00:03:40.811
She grabbed it, folded it, and put it in her pocket.

56
00:03:41.491 --> 00:03:44.173
Then the kids said good-bye and headed outside.

57
00:03:45.213 --> 00:03:50.216
The rainstorm that had left puddles in the street earlier had cleared away, and it was a warm,

58
00:03:50.456 --> 00:03:51.156
beautiful day.

59
00:03:51.176 --> 00:03:53.558
"So are we going to the zoo?"

60
00:03:53.898 --> 00:03:55.059
Darb asked eagerly.

61
00:03:55.079 --> 00:03:57.460
"We could," Gliss said.

62
00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:00.622
"But we should probably go to the palace first.

63
00:04:01.542 --> 00:04:05.484
Venna invited us to visit the next time we came to First City, remember?"

64
00:04:06.365 --> 00:04:09.707
Venna had been elected queen of Magica a few months earlier.

65
00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:14.489
Zann and his friends had helped her stop a plot to take over the government.

66
00:04:15.109 --> 00:04:18.011
Because of that, they were welcome at the palace anytime.

67
00:04:18.932 --> 00:04:22.153
Just then a large spotted rat raced past.

68
00:04:22.933 --> 00:04:24.574
Zing whistled and dashed after it.

69
00:04:25.254 --> 00:04:29.176
Zann was taken by surprise and ended up being dragged by the little dragon.

70
00:04:29.876 --> 00:04:32.217
Zann's friends laughed and chased both of them.

71
00:04:32.237 --> 00:04:34.918
"Zing, leave that poor rat alone!"

72
00:04:35.178 --> 00:04:35.799
Darb cried.

73
00:04:36.619 --> 00:04:39.540
Zann finally managed to yank his pet to a stop.

74
00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:43.002
"Now do you see why you weren't allowed to come with us today?"

75
00:04:43.422 --> 00:04:44.342
he said with a grin.

76
00:04:44.362 --> 00:04:48.384
"Who knows how many new creatures you would have decided to chase in Mistafar!"

77
00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.881
"Zing could use some exercise," Darb said.

78
00:04:51.901 --> 00:04:54.183
"Maybe we should take him to the park."

79
00:04:55.083 --> 00:04:55.884
Zann nodded.

80
00:04:56.524 --> 00:05:01.367
Wandering through one of the city's lovely parks with his friends sounded like a nice way to spend

81
00:05:01.407 --> 00:05:02.087
the afternoon.

82
00:05:02.928 --> 00:05:06.850
Gliss and Darb would probably hold hands and walk off by themselves.

83
00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:11.072
That would leave Zann with Perda, which sounded even nicer.

84
00:05:11.793 --> 00:05:14.514
But when he looked at Perda, she was shaking her head.

85
00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:17.376
"I have a better idea," she said.

86
00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.741
"Let's go to Wormwood."

87
00:05:20.622 --> 00:05:24.404
"Wormwood?" Gliss wrinkled her nose in distaste.

88
00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:26.486
"Ugh, why?"

89
00:05:26.506 --> 00:05:29.328
"I want to take a look at the tree."

90
00:05:30.248 --> 00:05:32.530
Perda pulled the blink image out of her pocket.

91
00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:35.592
"Maybe we can figure out what this riddle means.

92
00:05:36.052 --> 00:05:37.073
Wouldn't that be cool?"

93
00:05:37.974 --> 00:05:40.375
Zann traded a dubious look with Darb.

94
00:05:41.196 --> 00:05:46.019
Staring at the Wormwood tree didn't sound like a very good way to spend the last few hours

95
00:05:46.079 --> 00:05:46.980
of his friends' visit.

96
00:05:47.816 --> 00:05:52.178
"Well, Perda is the birthday girl," Darb said slowly.

97
00:05:53.199 --> 00:05:54.040
Gliss sighed.

98
00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:56.401
"That's true.

99
00:05:56.881 --> 00:05:58.922
She should get to choose what we do."

100
00:05:59.883 --> 00:06:00.963
She glanced at Perda.

101
00:06:00.983 --> 00:06:04.625
"Are you sure you really want to go to Wormwood?"

102
00:06:04.645 --> 00:06:08.227
"Absolutely." Perda smiled.

103
00:06:08.247 --> 00:06:10.028
"Thanks, you guys.

104
00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:11.429
I'll see you there!

105
00:06:11.849 --> 00:06:15.111
Zap." With a snap of her fingers, she disappeared.

106
00:06:15.931 --> 00:06:16.712
Zann shrugged.

107
00:06:17.432 --> 00:06:19.313
"Okay, let's go," he said to the others.

108
00:06:19.333 --> 00:06:23.235
"Maybe she'll get bored soon and we can spend the rest of the day at the zoo or

109
00:06:23.255 --> 00:06:23.755
the park."

110
00:06:24.596 --> 00:06:27.237
He made sure he was holding on tightly to Zing's leash.

111
00:06:27.898 --> 00:06:30.759
Then he snapped his fingers and zapped away.
